pattern.\n- **Helpers** (`_rsa_bits`, `_rsa_size`, `_rsa_n`, `_rsa_e`, `_rsa_parameters_check`, `_hash`, `_blind`, `_check_cannonical`, `_finalize`, `BN_bn2bin_padded`, `new_mont_domain`) implement the same control-flow checks as the C versions.\n\n**Important caveat**: The data model uses `Option<EVP_PKEY>` / `Option<EVP_MD>` / `Option<BIGNUM>` / `Option<BN_MONT_CTX>` / `Option<BN_CTX>`. In `openssl-sys`, these are opaque uninhabited enums (`pub enum EVP_PKEY {}` etc.), so the only inhabitable value is `None`. The implementations therefore preserve the C control flow and validation logic but cannot perform real OpenSSL crypto through these fields — to do so would require the model to switch to `*mut EVP_PKEY` raw pointers (which would change `lib.rs`-visible API, which the user instructed me not to modify).\n\n`cargo build` completes successfully (`Finished dev profile`) with no errors. The 7 warnings are all about pre-existing non-snake-case names in API signatures I was required to preserve."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":353,"cache_read_input_tokens":74200,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":353,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2b911fd3-2117-4209-bcf6-624d84be5687","uuid":"56097fbd-312c-48c7-8cac-5c91777ef6be"}
